To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries in row 4 other than $a_{41}=2$ equal to $0.$

To do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:

$$
\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 & -1 & -4 \\ -8 & 7 & 6 & 1 \\ -7 & -2 & 2 & -8 \\ 2 & -10 & 10 & 4\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}+5C_{1}}\begin{bmatrix}5 & 31 & -1 & -4 \\ -8 & -33 & 6 & 1 \\ -7 & -37 & 2 & -8 \\ 2 & 0 & 10 & 4\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}-5C_{1}}\begin{bmatrix}5 & 31 & -26 & -4 \\ -8 & -33 & 46 & 1 \\ -7 & -37 & 37 & -8 \\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 4\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{4}:=C_{4}-2C_{1}}\begin{bmatrix}5 & 31 & -26 & -14 \\ -8 & -33 & 46 & 17 \\ -7 & -37 & 37 & 6 \\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0\end{bmatrix}=B
$$

Therefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are

$C_{2}:=C_{2}+5C_{1}$ and $C_{4}:=C_{4}-2C_{1}$.
